 "text": "Hey, how's everything going? I like using a thin layer of fresh oil right after drying. Then varnish right after the oil is fully dry. Which usually takes an hour or two. Six months in a good temperature controlled box would give you the safety mark. It' the longest single step. You can try two weeks or so and call it win. Most modern oil paints these days dry pretty well after a week or so. It stop changing colour under the light, and the surface will feel smooth to the touch.",
